    "narrative": "Our lineup for May 13th is anchored by **Kyle Tucker** (67.29) and **Sam Antonacci** (64.49), our clear top-tier plays for this slate. **Kyle Tucker** thrives despite the matchup against Robbie Ray, buoyed by the high-upside park environment and a reliable slot in the order. Meanwhile, **Sam Antonacci** is a high-conviction start; his .391 xwOBA and favorable matchup against Seth Lugo\u2014combined with the efficiency boost from the leadoff spot\u2014make him an elite statistical play today. **Gunnar Henderson** (62.31) also merits strong consideration, as the combination of a hitter-friendly park and winds blowing out significantly outweighs the challenge of facing Fried, keeping him firmly in our \"Strong\" category.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved choosing between **Coby Mayo** (57.16) and **Brady House** (49.99). While **Brady House** held a solid base projection, his performance metrics dipped against the LHP Nick Lodolo, whereas **Coby Mayo** benefited from positive park factors and a dynamic platoon advantage that boosted his efficiency enough to justify his inclusion over both **Brady House** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (48.73). The decision to sit **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** was purely performance-driven; facing Griffin Jax with a lower projected efficiency meant he didn't quite crack the starting rotation today.\n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for several key contributors. Specifically, **Liam Hicks** (57.76), **Josh Jung** (53.52), **Jackson Merrill** (55.15), **Heliot Ramos** (41.12), and **Andy Pages** (54.51) all carry risks if their actual batting orders shift downward. **Heliot Ramos** is particularly high-risk; facing Shohei Ohtani (2.75 xERA) forces his score toward our floor. Conversely, **Drake Baldwin** (58.87) is a must-start at catcher, as his strong batting position (#2) effectively offsets the tough matchup against Shota Imanaga. As we continue to manage our games-played cap, we will keep **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** stashed on the IL, awaiting their return to help us make up ground in our SB-scarce environment.",
